      "lessons": [
        {
          "order": 1,
          "title": "Estilo y variación sintáctica",
          "theory_content": "El estilo avanzado combina frases cortas y largas para crear ritmo. Una frase corta enfatiza (He stopped.) y una larga desarrolla ideas con subordinadas. Varía el comienzo de las frases: no empieces todas con el sujeto. Usa participios y cláusulas de gerundio para condensar: Having finished the report, she left.",
          "theory_table": [
            {
              "label": "Corta",
              "value": "He stopped. Silence."
            },
            {
              "label": "Con participio",
              "value": "Having finished, she left."
            },
            {
              "label": "Con gerundio",
              "value": "Walking home, I thought of you."
            },
            {
              "label": "Inversión",
              "value": "Seldom had he felt so calm."
            }
          ],
          "practice_content": "Reescribe tres frases seguidas con distintos comienzos y longitudes.",
          "exercises": [
            {
              "type": "fill",
              "instruction": "Completa la frase.",
              "sentence": "___ finished the report, she left the office.",
              "answer": "Having",
              "hint": "Having + participio."
            },
            {
              "type": "choice",
              "q": "¿Qué frase varía mejor el ritmo?",
              "opts": [
                "He stopped. Silence filled the room.",
                "He he stopped.",
                "He stopped and he was silent and he looked around and he sat."
              ],
              "correct": 0,
              "why": "Corta + continuación."
            },
            {
              "type": "order",
              "instruction": "Ordena las palabras para formar la oración.",
              "words": [
                "thought",
                "I",
                "of",
                "Walking",
                "home",
                "you"
              ],
              "answer": "Walking home I thought of you",
              "hint": "Gerundio + coma + sujeto + verbo."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "order": 2,
          "title": "Recursos retóricos",
          "theory_content": "Los recursos retóricos dan fuerza al discurso: metaphor (Time is a thief), simile (as brave as a lion), tricolon (veni, vidi, vici: tres elementos), repetition (We shall fight on the beaches...) y rhetorical question (Who among us has not failed?). Úsalos con intención, no como adorno.",
          "theory_table": [
            {
              "label": "Metáfora",
              "value": "Time is a thief."
            },
            {
              "label": "Símil",
              "value": "as brave as a lion"
            },
            {
              "label": "Tricolon",
              "value": "veni, vidi, vici"
            },
            {
              "label": "Pregunta retórica",
              "value": "Who has not failed?"
            }
          ],
          "practice_content": "Escribe una frase con metáfora y otra con tricolon sobre tu ciudad.",
          "exercises": [
            {
              "type": "fill",
              "instruction": "Completa la frase.",
              "sentence": "'Time is a thief' is an example of a ___. (metáfora)",
              "answer": "metaphor",
              "hint": "Metaphor = metáfora."
            },
            {
              "type": "choice",
              "q": "¿Qué es un tricolon?",
              "opts": [
                "una comparación con like",
                "una pregunta",
                "tres elementos en serie"
              ],
              "correct": 2,
              "why": "Serie de tres."
            },
            {
              "type": "order",
              "instruction": "Ordena las palabras para formar la oración.",
              "words": [
                "failed",
                "among",
                "has",
                "Who",
                "not",
                "us"
              ],
              "answer": "Who among us has not failed",
              "hint": "Pregunta retórica."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "order": 3,
          "title": "Ambigüedad y matiz",
          "theory_content": "Los matices cambian el significado: hedging (suavizar afirmaciones) como seems, tends to, arguably; y énfasis como undoubtedly, clearly. Un texto C2 gestiona ambos: The results arguably suggest... frente a The results clearly show... Cuidado con la ambigüedad no deseada: Visiting relatives can be boring (¿visitar o los familiares que visitan?).",
          "theory_table": [
            {
              "label": "Hedging",
              "value": "It tends to rain in April."
            },
            {
              "label": "Énfasis",
              "value": "This is undoubtedly true."
            },
            {
              "label": "Ambigüedad",
              "value": "Visiting relatives can be boring."
            },
            {
              "label": "Matiz",
              "value": "arguably the best"
            }
          ],
          "practice_content": "Reescribe una afirmación tajante con hedging.",
          "exercises": [
            {
              "type": "fill",
              "instruction": "Completa la frase.",
              "sentence": "The results ___ suggest a link. (posiblemente)",
              "answer": "arguably",
              "hint": "Arguably = posiblemente."
            },
            {
              "type": "choice",
              "q": "¿Qué frase suaviza mejor?",
              "opts": [
                "It never fails.",
                "It is obviously perfect.",
                "It seems to be effective."
              ],
              "correct": 2,
              "why": "Seems to suaviza."
            },
            {
              "type": "order",
              "instruction": "Ordena las palabras para formar la oración.",
              "words": [
                "a",
                "This",
                "is",
                "great",
                "undoubtedly",
                "success"
              ],
              "answer": "This is undoubtedly a great success",
              "hint": "Adverbio de énfasis."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "order": 4,
          "title": "Registro literario y corrección de estilo",
          "theory_content": "El registro literario usa imágenes, vocabulario evocador y sintaxis elaborada: The sun bled into the horizon. Para corregir estilo: elimina redundancias (revert back → revert), cambia verbos débiles (make a decision → decide), prefiere voz activa y suprime muletillas (very, really). Lee en voz alta para notar el ritmo.",
          "theory_table": [
            {
              "label": "Redundancia",
              "value": "revert back → revert"
            },
            {
              "label": "Verbo fuerte",
              "value": "make a decision → decide"
            },
            {
              "label": "Voz activa",
              "value": "Mistakes were made → We made mistakes."
            },
            {
              "label": "Imagen",
              "value": "The sun bled into the horizon."
            }
          ],
          "practice_content": "Edita este fragmento eliminando tres redundancias y reforzando verbos.",
          "exercises": [
            {
              "type": "fill",
              "instruction": "Completa la frase.",
              "sentence": "'Make a decision' is more concise as '___'.",
              "answer": "decide",
              "hint": "Verbo fuerte."
            },
            {
              "type": "choice",
              "q": "¿Cuál es una redundancia?",
              "opts": [
                "go back",
                "revert",
                "revert back"
              ],
              "correct": 2,
              "why": "Revert ya implica back."
            },
            {
              "type": "order",
              "instruction": "Ordena las palabras para formar la oración.",
              "words": [
                "us",
                "made",
                "by",
                "Mistakes",
                "were"
              ],
              "answer": "Mistakes were made by us",
              "hint": "Ordena la frase en voz pasiva."
            }
          ]
        }
